WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.328 --> 00:00:06.339
Over the last decade and a half, we’ve moved
from describing cancer as it appears under

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:11.669
the microscope to a molecular diagnosis of
a cancer that’s based on the changes in

00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:12.669
the genome.

00:00:12.669 --> 00:00:18.809
Next generation sequencing technologies have
allowed us to discover those genetic abnormalities

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:26.669
at a dizzying rate, generating terabytes and
petabytes of data that overwhelm the ability

00:00:26.669 --> 00:00:31.429
of most cancer researchers to wrangle and
understand.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:38.109
There’s just too much data, it’s in too
many places, and it’s too diverse.

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:43.359
With the genomic data commons it will be much
easier to get the data and to analyze it at

00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:44.779
the scale they need.

00:00:44.779 --> 00:00:50.129
One of the really important parts of the genomic
data commons is having the ability for every

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:57.349
time a data submission happens, to analyze
it in exactly the same way and harmonize those

00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:01.778
data with all the other data that's been submitted
to the genomic data commons.

00:01:01.778 --> 00:01:03.838
There's no other resource out there like it.

00:01:03.838 --> 00:01:09.919
We can compare our data from our patients,
to data that came in through The Cancer Genome

00:01:09.919 --> 00:01:12.719
Atlas studies, from many other studies.

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:19.909
We will be able to do a lot of analysis without
having to download a lot of data.

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:22.808
We’ll be able to analyze it online.

00:01:22.808 --> 00:01:28.588
The GDC is an essential tool if we are going
to understand the data we collect, get the

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:32.698
information we need out of it, to improve
the way we treat cancer.

00:01:32.698 --> 00:01:37.289
The GDC provides an exciting new opportunity
for cancer researchers.

00:01:37.289 --> 00:01:44.268
They will be able to upload their own data
to the GDC and therefore use all the bioinformatics

00:01:44.268 --> 00:01:48.369
tools that are present in the GDC to understand
their own data.

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:52.999
But also, to see how it relates to all of
the other data.

00:01:52.999 --> 00:01:59.619
Over time this will also increase the size
and the number of cases that are present in

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.619
the GDC, giving us greater statistical power.

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:09.778
We can start to do a much better job of tailoring
specific therapies, specific treatments for

00:02:09.778 --> 00:02:13.418
a patient based on the experience we see with
other patients.

00:02:13.418 --> 00:02:18.739
You can’t overestimate the power of this
tool to help us us understand how to manage

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:25.568
our patients, what drugs to give them, and
as this grows, whether they are going to respond

00:02:25.568 --> 00:02:27.198
to these drugs or not.

00:02:27.198 --> 00:02:28.388
This is going to help us all.

00:02:28.388 --> 00:02:33.998
The genomic information is really life or
death to our patients, it makes such a big

00:02:33.998 --> 00:02:34.468
difference.

